{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>To whom He said.</b> The prophet." "<b>This.</b> Jerusalem — it is your rest. Make rest for the weary, so that he not flee to Egypt and Assyria." "<b>The resting-place.</b> From the root מרגוע (Jeremiah 6:15); both are nouns. According to the Jerusalem grammarian, the word is a verb." "The alef at the end of <b>אבוא</b> is added like the alef of ההלכוא (Joshua 10:24)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:36.282751111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}